===Etymology===
After {{w|Ebola river}} (area of discovery of type species) {{suffix||virus|lang=mul}}. Reports conflict about who initially coined the name: either Karl Johnson of the American Centers for Disease Control<ref name="hz">{{cite book| title={{w|The Hot Zone}} |last=Preston |first=Richard |author={{w|Richard Preston}} |page=117 |text=Karl Johnson named it Ebola |publisher=Anchor Books ([[Random House]]) |date=July 20, 1995}}</ref> or Belgian researchers.<ref name="observer">{{cite web |url=http://www.theguardian.com/world/2014/oct/04/ebola-zaire-peter-piot-outbreak?utm_source=digg&utm_medium=email |title='In 1976 I Discovered Ebola&nbsp;– Now I Fear an Unimaginable Tragedy' |last1=Bredow |first1=Rafaela von |last2=Hackenbroch |first2=Veronika |work=[[The Observer]] |publisher=[[Guardian Media Group]] |date=4 October 2014}}</ref>

